# Omarchy Server package list, pacstrapped by the ISO for the server edition.
# The ISO builder also reads this file when constructing the offline mirror.
#
# Derived from omarchy-base.packages by subtraction: the compositor, the shell,
# GUI applications, the audio/bluetooth/printing stacks, fonts beyond the
# console, and the capture pipeline all come out. What stays is the CLI, the TUI
# toolbox, containers, networking, security, and the theming plumbing that the
# terminal side of a theme needs.
#
# Only eight entries are not in omarchy-base.packages. Keep that true, or teach
# test/shell.d/server-packages-test.sh about the new one:
#   openssh              - the desktop gets it from the ISO's archinstall.packages, and
#                          the server edition cannot assume that list.
#   rsync                - the transport a headless box is administered over.
#   lazyjournal          - the [L] door. The desktop reads logs in a window; a server
#                          reads them in the terminal it is already in.
#   dua-cli              - disk usage analyzer, CLI replacement for baobab
#   lazydocker           - Docker TUI for the [D] door
#   mkinitcpio-dropbear  - SSH server in initramfs for remote LUKS unlock
#   mkinitcpio-netconf   - network configuration in initramfs
#   mkinitcpio-utils     - utilities for initramfs (including encryptssh hook)

